WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:13.745
You probably recognize my face—or at least my golden mask.

2
00:00:13.746 --> 00:00:22.367
Most people know me as King Tut from ancient Egypt.

3
00:00:22.368 --> 00:00:26.633
But my real name is Tutankhamun. I became an

4
00:00:26.633 --> 00:00:30.706
Egyptian pharaoh, or king, when I

5
00:00:30.706 --> 00:00:35.277
was about nine years old. But my reign was not long. I was only

6
00:00:35.277 --> 00:00:38.563
19 when I died from an

7
00:00:38.563 --> 00:00:43.280
unknown cause. My people buried me in a tomb in the

8
00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:47.305
Valley of the Kings. That's where many other pharaohs were buried. I

9
00:00:47.305 --> 00:00:51.489
was an important king, and I made

10
00:00:51.489 --> 00:00:56.270
many big changes to Egypt. But people soon forgot about me, and I

11
00:00:56.270 --> 00:01:02.967
was lost for over three thousand years! Then, in 1922, a British archaeologist named Howard

12
00:01:02.967 --> 00:01:11.309
Carter discovered my tomb. Carter and his team were amazed by

13
00:01:11.309 --> 00:01:14.611
what they found. The rooms of my tomb were filled

14
00:01:14.611 --> 00:01:20.455
with thousands of objects. That was because we ancient Egyptians believed

15
00:01:20.456 --> 00:01:25.629
the dead needed things for the afterlife. With me, I had golden chariots,

16
00:01:25.629 --> 00:01:31.863
furniture, food, wine—even underwear! My coffin was made of solid

17
00:01:31.863 --> 00:01:36.486
gold. It took Carter ten years to

18
00:01:36.486 --> 00:01:43.947
remove everything from my tomb. People were excited about Carter's discovery.

19
00:01:43.948 --> 00:01:47.543
Mine was the most complete pharaoh's

20
00:01:47.543 --> 00:01:51.660
tomb ever found. Other tombs had been robbed of

21
00:01:51.660 --> 00:01:55.598
valuable objects. In fact, robbers had actually

22
00:01:55.599 --> 00:01:59.242
broken into my tomb twice! But they weren't able to

23
00:01:59.251 --> 00:02:02.056
steal very much. The contents of my tomb

24
00:02:02.056 --> 00:02:06.301
were displayed at the Egyptian Museum in Cairo. Later some objects traveled across

25
00:02:06.301 --> 00:02:11.356
the world. In 1939, two of my

26
00:02:11.356 --> 00:02:18.137
trumpets were played on the radio. I hope the audience

27
00:02:18.138 --> 00:02:20.536
enjoyed the concert. I heard that 150

28
00:02:20.536 --> 00:02:25.507
million people were listening! The most famous treasure

29
00:02:25.508 --> 00:02:30.235
from my tomb was the golden mask on my mummy. Originally, this mask wasn't

30
00:02:30.235 --> 00:02:33.819
meant for me at all! It had first

31
00:02:33.819 --> 00:02:37.987
been made for a different pharaoh. But when I

32
00:02:37.987 --> 00:02:41.655
died, it was used on me instead. The mask had

33
00:02:41.655 --> 00:02:47.172
to be changed though. The original owner's

34
00:02:47.173 --> 00:02:52.668
face was removed from the front of the mask. Then a new

35
00:02:52.669 --> 00:02:56.640
face that looked like mine was placed on the mask. My name

36
00:02:56.641 --> 00:03:00.387
was written over the original owner's name. Other objects—maybe

37
00:03:00.388 --> 00:03:05.534
even the tomb itself—were probably meant for someone else too. Most pharaohs

38
00:03:05.535 --> 00:03:09.570
had large, grand tombs. But mine

39
00:03:09.570 --> 00:03:13.718
is small and simple. Archaeologists think

40
00:03:13.719 --> 00:03:17.233
my death was sudden and unexpected. So

41
00:03:17.234 --> 00:03:21.085
they believe a grander tomb wasn't ready when I died. Today

42
00:03:21.085 --> 00:03:26.062
I'm known as the most famous pharaoh from ancient Egypt. But

43
00:03:26.063 --> 00:03:29.064
much about me still remains a mystery. For

44
00:03:29.064 --> 00:03:32.740
example, nobody is exactly sure how I died. Maybe

45
00:03:32.740 --> 00:03:36.814
one day someone will find out.

46
00:03:36.815 --> 00:03:41.739
I believe people will be interested in my life for many years to come.

47
00:03:41.739 --> 00:03:46.487
I have plenty of secrets waiting to be discovered!

